<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adolf II, Prince of Schaumburg-Lippe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1883–1936</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adolf II was the last reigning prince of Schaumburg-Lippe, a small state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>, succeeding his father George in 1911. He abdicated in November 1918 during the German Revolution, and the state continued as the Free State of Schaumburg-Lippe. He and his wife died in an air crash in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> in 1936.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adolf-ii-prince-of-schaumburg-lippe.jpg" alt="Adolf II, Prince of Schaumburg-Lippe" width="320" height="466" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nicola Perscheid · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adolf_II,_Prince_of_Schaumburg-Lippe_c1917.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
